From eebd8c69465c247ba09a6d891acf4f3f9151b014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZeroCode321 <ZeroCode321@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:20:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(chest): host-side plugin and skill vault

A chest holds two kinds of real artifact rather than text a model is asked to
pretend with: plugin packages it can install into the booted profile, and
SKILL.md files under the user skill root that the harness's own skill provider
discovers. Both export to one `.chest` document for sharing, and both import
back.

The gateway scans the store, the registered external folders, the skill root,
and the profile manifest on every read; one serialized queue owns every
mutation; the profile edits an install makes are a `link:` dependency, the
bundle name in `dsh.profile.bundles`, and the `node_modules` link.
